meta {
  name: Get TMDB Person Films
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{API_URL}}/tmdb/person/287?kind=actor
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  kind: actor
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{CLERK_TOKEN}}
}

docs {
  Get a person's released films with their IMDb ratings, filtered for the person modal.

  Requires CLERK_TOKEN (returns 401 without it), as each film costs an OMDb request.

  Path Parameters:
  - tmdbPersonId: TMDB person ID - REQUIRED

  Query Parameters:
  - kind: actor or director - REQUIRED
    - actor: credited acting roles (roles marked "(uncredited)" are left out)
    - director: films where the person's job is Director

  Films already in the collection are left out, as the modal lists those from the
  database. Any other film is left out when it:
  - has no release date, or one in the future
  - doesn't have the status "Released" on TMDB
  - has no IMDb ID or no IMDb rating
  - has fewer than 1,000 IMDb votes
  - fails its lookup, or isn't reached within the 20-second time budget

  Returns { data: { films: [...], hiddenCount } }, newest first. hiddenCount is
  how many films outside the collection were left out. Each film has:
  - tmdbId: TMDB movie ID
  - title: Film title
  - year: Release year
  - character: Role played, joined with " / " for several roles; actors only, null when unknown
  - imdbId, imdbRating, imdbVotes: from OMDb (www.omdbapi.com), which is unofficial,
    so figures can differ slightly from imdb.com

  Returns 400 for a bad ID or kind, 404 when TMDB has no such person, and 502
  when OMDb rejects the API key or every film lookup fails. Saves nothing.

  Example Response:
  {
    "data": {
      "films": [
        {
          "tmdbId": "550",
          "title": "Fight Club",
          "year": 1999,
          "character": "Tyler Durden",
          "imdbId": "tt0137523",
          "imdbRating": 8.8,
          "imdbVotes": 2400000
        }
      ],
      "hiddenCount": 12
    }
  }
}
